    "scenesThatPass": [
      "VICTORIA: I do not now remember when I first knew I was different.\nVICTORIA: Or rather, that my life belonged to others, besides myself.\nVICTORIA: I must have been about eleven, or thereabouts, when they left a book open on the nursery table.\nVICTORIA: And so I learned I was nearer to the Crown than I had thought...",
      "LEHZEN: Next time, do as I say.\nLADY FLORA: Hurry, scurry, to the little Princess.",
      "VICTORIA: Well, if it’s a wasted journey they can’t blame me.\nLEHZEN: Your mother wants you downstairs.",
      "VICTORIA: I don’t think so.\nDUCHESS OF KENT: It’s a nice day for a walk.\nVICTORIA: If you wish, Mama.",
      "VICTORIA: How is she?\nLEHZEN: She wants to leave tonight but they’ve persuaded her to stay until the morning. She’s asked for your bed to be set up in her room. I’ll see …\nVICTORIA: Must I? Can’t I be alone for one solitary night?\nVICTORIA: Why does everyone fight over me?"
    ]
  },
